OBJECTIVE:

1. Understand branching and merging.
2. Create a new branch.
3. Make changes in the branch.
4. Merge the branch with master.
5. Understand branch and merge requests in GitLab.

PREREQUISITE:

Git environment with P4Merge installed and configured.


--------------------------------------------------
BRANCHING
--------------------------------------------------

1. Create a new branch called GitNewBranch

git branch GitNewBranch


2. List all local and remote branches

git branch -a

The * symbol shows the current branch.


3. Switch to the new branch

git checkout GitNewBranch

OR:

git switch GitNewBranch


4. Create a new file

touch newfile.txt


5. Add some content

echo "This is my new branch" > newfile.txt


6. Check the files

ls


7. Check Git status

git status


8. Add the file

git add newfile.txt


9. Commit the changes

git commit -m "Added changes in GitNewBranch"


10. Check status again

git status


--------------------------------------------------
MERGING
--------------------------------------------------

1. Switch back to master

git checkout master


2. List differences between master and GitNewBranch

git diff master GitNewBranch


3. View visual differences using P4Merge

git difftool master GitNewBranch

P4Merge will display the visual differences.


4. Merge GitNewBranch into master

git merge GitNewBranch


5. Check the commit history

git log --oneline --graph --decorate


6. Delete the branch after merging

git branch -d GitNewBranch


7. Check branches

git branch -a


8. Check final status

git status


--------------------------------------------------
IMPORTANT COMMANDS
--------------------------------------------------

git branch GitNewBranch
        → Creates a new branch

git branch -a
        → Lists local and remote branches

git checkout GitNewBranch
        → Switches to the new branch

git status
        → Shows current repository status

git add .
        → Stages changes

git commit -m "message"
        → Saves changes to the branch

git checkout master
        → Switches to master

git diff master GitNewBranch
        → Shows differences between branches

git difftool master GitNewBranch
        → Shows visual differences using P4Merge

git merge GitNewBranch
        → Merges the branch into master

git log --oneline --graph --decorate
        → Shows commit history as a graph

git branch -d GitNewBranch
        → Deletes the merged branch


